From: Mehmet Salih <salihmehmet497@gmail.com>
Subject: net: airoha: add Airoha EN7523 SoC support

Consolidated EN7523 (dual Cortex-A53 in AArch32, EN7581-lineage frame
engine/QDMA/PPE) support, every item verified on a Zyxel EX3501-T0:

- EN7523 SoC data (single PPE, 8 TX / 16 RX rings, no xfp-mac reset);
- TX queue selection wraps into the 8 backed rings, every TX ring stays
  on TX IRQ queue 0;
- write REG_RX_CPU_IDX right after REG_RX_DMA_IDX with a dma_wmb(),
  larger RX rings, honour soc->max_rx_ring;
- deassert the GDMA reset, HW_FWD_DSCP_CFG/HW_DSCP_NUM/INGRESS_TRTCM,
  GLOBAL_CFG and the undocumented 0x102c/0x00fc/0x0030 bits as on the
  stock firmware, PSE page reservations scaled for the smaller PSE;
- RX source port from msg1 bits 24..20 (0x10 | switch port) mapped to a
  DSA metadata dst; the switch special tag travels in the descriptor
  (see the mt7530 patch), GDM1 INGRESS_CFG = STAG_EN|FC_EN|BIT(2);
- no hardware checksum/TSO/LRO offload (the stock firmware does not use
  it either);
- FE LAN/WAN MAC range registers cover base..base+15 so the PPE treats
  frames for the bridge/WAN MACs as "for me";
- PPE initialised from the CPU (no NPU object on this SoC) with the
  stock register values, PPE fields of the RX descriptor decoded with
  the EN7523 layout (15-bit FOE index, reason at bits 19..15), the NPU
  cores booted directly from the reserved firmware region, and the
  QDMA rings placed in the "eth-ring-buf" shared-dma-pool.
